 kit trust - trusts a clone, so kit runs what it asks for there

   one of
   *kit trust*  trusts a clone, so kit runs what it asks for there

     --yes    records the trust without asking, as a CI job does for its own checkout

     <path>   a clone, or a directory in one, the clone here when none is given; or a folder ending
              in /

   --list     prints the clones and the folders you trust, one per line
   --check    prints the name the clone is trusted by, and exits 0 when it is trusted, as it asks
              now, and 1 when not; it asks nothing and runs nothing of the clone's, for a screen
              that asks for the trust itself
   --asks     prints what the clone asks kit to run, one line each, as kit trust shows it, and asks
              nothing
   --revoke   takes the trust of a clone or a folder back


 kit trust
